# Local dev secrets for the digest worker (pi-ai via Cloudflare AI Gateway).
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (which is gitignored) and fill in the values:
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# Then run:  bunx wrangler dev --port 8792 --persist-to ../../.wrangler-state
# and trigger:  curl "http://127.0.0.1:8792/run?lang=en"
#
# NOTE: CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID and CLOUDFLARE_GATEWAY_ID now live in
# wrangler.jsonc `vars` (so CI sets them on deploy, and local dev picks them up
# automatically). The ONLY value you must provide here is CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY.

# ── CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY (the only required secret) ────────────────────────
# An API TOKEN (used as a bearer token by pi-ai), NOT your global API key.
# Dashboard → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token → Custom token, with:
#   • Account › Workers AI › Read + Run   (to invoke models)
# Scope it to this account. Paste the generated token below.
CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=""

# ── Optional overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment to override the wrangler.jsonc vars for local dev only:
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""
# CLOUDFLARE_GATEWAY_ID=""

# Guards the manual /run endpoint (Authorization: Bearer <token>). Leave empty
# to allow unauthenticated /run in local dev.
DIGEST_TRIGGER_TOKEN=""

# Override the model (defaults to the value in wrangler.jsonc). Must exist in
# pi-ai's cloudflare-ai-gateway catalog. Workers-AI models usable with only
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY:
#   workers-ai/@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6      (default)
#   workers-ai/@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5
#   workers-ai/@cf/zai-org/glm-5.2
#   workers-ai/@cf/zai-org/glm-4.7-flash
#   workers-ai/@cf/nvidia/nemotron-3-120b-a12b
# DIGEST_MODEL="workers-ai/@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6"
